>> title: Pineapple Bun
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bun, chinese, hong kong, enriched, oven
>> counters: Bakery, Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: bo lo bao, bolo bao, boh loh bao, 菠蘿包, pineapple bun, pineapple bread, pineapple-top bun
>> pairs-with: japanese-milk-bread
>> servings: 8
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the lid cracks only if it is drier than the dough under it, and one worked warm or rolled thin bakes smooth instead
>> step.1: cook to a paste, cool it
>> step.2: mix into the tangzhong and knead 10 min
>> step.3: knead the butter in, rise until doubled
>> step.4: cream the lid and work the flour in
>> step.5: portion the dough, drape a lid on each, proof 45 min
>> step.6: brush and bake 350°F (175°C) 16 min

Cook @bread flour{2%Tbs}(16 g) with @whole milk{1/3%cup}(80 mL) in a #saucepan{} over low heat, whisking, until it thickens to a paste, then ~cool{20%min} to room temperature.

Mix @bread flour{2 1/4%cup}(300 g), @granulated sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @nonfat dry milk{2%Tbs}(14 g), @instant yeast{2%tsp}(6 g), @egg{1%large}, @warm whole milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL) and @table salt{1%tsp}(6 g) into @&(~1)tangzhong{}, then knead ~knead{10%min} to a smooth, slack dough.

Knead @softened unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(40 g) into @&(~1)dough{} until it is glossy again, then cover and ~rise{1%hr} until doubled.

Cream @softened unsalted butter{5%Tbs}(70 g) and @lard{2%Tbs}(25 g) with @powdered sugar{2/3%cup}(80 g), @egg yolk{1%large}, @custard powder{1%Tbs}(8 g) and @baker's ammonia{1/2%tsp}(2 g), then work @cake flour{1%cup}(120 g) in to a stiff, rollable paste.

Divide @&(~2)risen dough{} into eight balls, roll @&(~1)lid paste{} into eight discs between sheets of paper and drape one over each ball, then ~proof{45%min} until light.

Brush @&(~1)draped buns{} with @beaten egg yolk{1%large} and bake in a 350°F (175°C) #oven{} for ~bake{16%min}, until the grid has opened and gone deep gold.
